      "confidence": "high for source behavior; conditional operational consequence",
      "title": "Use the configured mapping revision when accepting CES cached grants",
      "path": "src/main/java/com/scb/auth/login/entitlement/cache/RedisEntitlementCacheService.java",
      "line_start": 120,
      "line_end": 124,
      "side": "right",
      "trigger": "A user has cached CES grants. An operator restricts role mappings or allowed actions, sets EMS3_MAPPING_VERSION to a successor, and restarts with the same Redis.",
      "baseline": "main has no CES functional projection or this cache. Existing EMS2 behavior is not claimed to be regression-tested.",
      "candidate": "The cache key always uses Constant.EMS3_DATA_ROLE_MAPPING_VERSION. get() validates source/payload only. Ems3LegacyEntitlementService.get returns cached grants before the changed mapper runs. The exported mapping version is never consumed.",
      "consequence": "The old role/actions can remain in new authentication responses until the cached projection expires. Shipped TTL is 3600 seconds. This can preserve an action removed by the mapping update.",
      "owner": "unknown",
      "next_action": "Partition or invalidate functional projection caches by the effective configured mapping revision, and reject an envelope from a different revision. Add a focused old-cache/new-mapping assertion.",
